Negative control for the ONE-writer law (T1.4 falsifiability).

Gives `useCriteriaUrlSync` a SECOND query-string writer: its own
`useUrlSearchParams` bag, the shape it carried before the conversion. Both bags
rebuild the WHOLE query string from their own state, so each one's write-back
deletes every param the other owns — last one wins. Nothing looks broken at the
call site: the criteria params are all still written, and the surface state (or
the filter, depending which bag commits last) simply evaporates a tick later.

This is the exact defect `usePlaygroundUrlState` exists to prevent (`D3`/`T8`,
`AC9.1`, `S11`), and the one its own docblock names: "Two `useUrlSearchParams`
instances each rebuild the whole query string from their own state, so the
second would delete every param the first owns on its next write." The mutant is
planted in the consumer that was converted rather than in the writer itself — a
regression here is a revert of one seam, not a rewrite.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: all three of the writer spec's one-writer cases — a criteria write and a
surface write in the same tick both survive, in EITHER order, and a later
criteria write does not clobber the surface state it does not own.

Mechanism note, not an assertion hint. The clobber signature is now the MIRROR
of the pre-fix one: the playground bag commits its merged patch on a macrotask,
which lands AFTER the criteria bag's own write-back, so it is the criteria param
that is erased and the six surface params that survive. Either side being empty
is the same defect — two writers, last one wins — and the side that loses is
only a function of which bag commits last.

A second writer that clobbers through `router.replace` INSIDE the criteria
watcher (this control's pre-fix shape) no longer falsifies anything and was NOT
carried over: the write queue heals it. The router's `history.replaceState` lands
in microtasks, the queue's commit is the macrotask after it, and that commit
re-stamps the whole bag — surface params included — so the clobber is undone
before the spec ever reads `window.location`. Proven GREEN 2026-08-12 (63 passed
| 3 skipped, the same as an unpatched tree) before this control was re-authored.
That is a property of the fix, not a blind spot in the harness: a co-scheduled
second writer is genuinely harmless now, and only a writer whose write is the
LAST word can still clobber.

